== Mock Examination 2 — Questions

#mcq(1, [The number of autosomes in a human gamete is], [23], [22], [44], [46])

#mcq(2, [In a dihybrid cross, the F2 generation has how many phenotypes when both genes show complete dominance?], [2], [3], [9], [4])

#mcq(3, [Polygenic inheritance produces], [continuous variation], [discontinuous variation], [sex-linked traits only], [only harmful effects])

#mcq(4, [Divergent evolution means that], [unrelated species come to look alike], [species stop evolving], [related species become different], [a species becomes extinct])

#mcq(5, [A population of 400 animals loses 60 births, 40 deaths, 30 immigrants and 50 emigrants in a year. The new size is], [360], [420], [380], [440])

#mcq(6, [The ten per cent law is a statement about], [the number of species], [the rate of photosynthesis], [the size of a population], [energy transfer between trophic levels])

#mcq(7, [Which is a seral stage of a hydrosere?], [Reed swamp], [Bare rock], [Desert], [Montane forest])

#mcq(8, [A gene bank protects], [habitats], [genetic material of many varieties], [only large animals], [rivers])

#mcq(9, [A resistant crop variety controls a disease by], [killing the pathogen chemically], [preventing the pathogen from infecting the plant], [removing the vector], [increasing rainfall])

#mcq(10, [If an anomalous point appears on a graph, you should], [move it to fit the line], [join it to the next point], [mark it and explain it, then draw the best-fit line through the trend], [ignore the whole graph])

#mcq(11, [In the cross Tt × Tt, the expected genotypic ratio is], [3 : 1], [1 : 1], [2 : 1], [1 : 2 : 1])

#mcq(12, [Which of these is *not* a source of genetic variation?], [Mitosis], [Crossing over], [Independent assortment], [Mutation])

#mcq(13, [A mangrove tree excretes salt through its leaves. This is], [a structural adaptation], [a behavioural adaptation], [a physiological adaptation], [acclimatisation])

#mcq(14, [Analogous structures arise from], [common ancestry], [identical genes], [vestigial organs], [similar selection pressures in unrelated organisms])

#mcq(15, [Ecologists sample a habitat rather than counting every organism because], [it is faster and less damaging to the habitat], [counting is inaccurate], [sampling is always exact], [counting is illegal])

#mcq(16, [The relationship between a cow and the bacteria in its rumen is], [parasitism], [mutualism], [commensalism], [competition])

#mcq(17, [Carbon dioxide makes up about what fraction of the atmosphere?], [4 %], [0.04 %], [21 %], [78 %])

#mcq(18, [Shelter belts reduce erosion by], [increasing rainfall], [adding fertiliser], [reducing wind speed at ground level], [raising soil temperature])

#mcq(19, [The rumen of a ruminant is best described as], [a fermentation vat containing microbes], [an acid digestion chamber], [a water-absorbing organ], [a grinding gizzard])

#mcq(20, [The eyepiece of a microscope is also called the], [objective], [condenser], [diaphragm], [ocular lens])

#mcq(21, [The study of inheritance is called], [ecology], [genetics], [taxonomy], [physiology])

#mcq(22, [A pedigree shows two unaffected parents with an affected daughter. The condition is most likely], [autosomal recessive], [autosomal dominant], [X-linked recessive], [Y-linked])

#mcq(23, [Which process produces genetic variation during sexual reproduction?], [Binary fission], [Budding], [Vegetative propagation], [Crossing over and independent assortment])

#mcq(24, [Fish fins and dolphin flippers are analogous because they], [share a common ancestor], [contain the same bones], [have the same function but different origins], [are both vestigial])

#mcq(25, [The correct order of ecological levels, smallest to largest, is], [population, organism, community, ecosystem], [organism, population, community, ecosystem], [community, population, ecosystem, organism], [ecosystem, community, organism, population])

#mcq(26, [A pyramid of biomass may invert briefly because], [biomass is not measurable], [producers are always small], [plankton are eaten as fast as they multiply], [consumers do not respire])

#mcq(27, [The Haber process is an industrial form of], [denitrification], [nitrification], [ammonification], [nitrogen fixation])

#mcq(28, [Which of these is a secondary pollutant of acid rain?], [Sulphuric acid], [Sulphur dioxide], [Coal], [Smoke])

#mcq(29, [The advantage of organic manure over fertiliser in sandy soil is that manure], [improves water-holding capacity], [raises the pH at once], [supplies nitrogen instantly], [is sterile])

#mcq(30, [A cell 0.05 mm in diameter is drawn 10 mm across. The magnification is], [×20], [×2000], [×2], [×200])

#mcq(31, [A homozygous dominant genotype is written], [Tt], [TT], [tt], [T])

#mcq(32, [The ratio 9 : 3 : 3 : 1 in the F2 of a dihybrid cross was used by Mendel to show], [segregation], [linkage], [independent assortment], [mutation])

#mcq(33, [The mutation that causes sickle-cell anaemia changes], [the shape of the red cell membrane], [the number of chromosomes], [one amino acid in the haemoglobin chain], [the sex of the person])

#mcq(34, [Which statement would a Darwinian *not* accept?], [Variation arises at random], [An organ grows because it is used], [Selection favours the better adapted], [Only inherited variation matters])

#mcq(35, [Which of these describes a community rather than a population?], [All the organisms in a pond], [All the weaver birds in a tree], [All the mango trees on a farm], [All the tilapia in a lake])

#mcq(36, [A lichen is a mutualistic association between], [a bacterium and a fungus], [two fungi], [an alga and a moss], [an alga and a fungus])

#mcq(37, [The first plants to grow after a forest fire belong to], [secondary succession], [primary succession], [climax vegetation], [the pioneer stage on bare rock])

#mcq(38, [Which of these is *not* a pollutant?], [Sewage], [Carbon monoxide], [Water vapour from a kettle], [Lead in petrol])

#mcq(39, [The main storage pest of dried maize is], [the tsetse fly], [the weevil], [the mosquito], [the tick])

#mcq(40, [Increasing the magnification of a microscope], [increases the field of view], [does not change the field], [increases the brightness], [decreases the field of view])

